# Machine-specific packages: bootloader, firmware, GPU, network hardware and
# the greeter.
#
# Unlike the other applists, this file's CONTENTS are gitignored — they differ
# per machine and are not portable. Only this .example template is committed,
# so the concept is versioned even though the package names are not.
#
# Nothing installs from this file. By the time these dotfiles are cloned the
# machine has already booted, so its bootloader, microcode and drivers are
# necessarily present; and being gitignored, the file does not exist on a fresh
# clone anyway. Its only job is to tell package_report that these packages are
# tracked, so they stop showing up as untracked noise. Same arrangement as
# applist-local.
#
# On a new machine: copy this to applist-machine and fill it in with whatever
# that box needs.
#
# cp applist-machine.example applist-machine
#
# Example entries (this machine's, as a starting point):
#
# grub
# efibootmgr
# intel-ucode
# nvidia-open
# nvidia-settings
# iwd
# greetd
# greetd-tuigreet
